// The first Truth Scavenger Hunt, the First Moment of Truth (the
// last-chance filing window, the results one question at a time) and the
// bottle (Truth or Dare) between the questions.
//
// Trabolta needs facts. They are obscure, un-googleable, and in the
// Desktop's books: each answer is printed on a document carrying a codex
// QR (generated/questions.loom, from facts.json), so a program who finds
// one can prove it on their phone — and hold it, and trade it. The
// questions are also in everyone's Quest Log (`Hunt One`, generated too).
// All the beats are public, in the Desktop's room. Every filing on the 📝
// card is judged by the server (facts.json); the results are read here
// and settled by main.loom (+50, or marked for a guess).

// V4 / V5 — `start_the_hunt`. Trabolta reads round 1 (H1–H3) from the
// generated `Hunt One Questions`, which hands back to `Hunt One Go`
// (every divert is the last item of its beat, so the chain is the same
// under the Sim and a true divert).
== Truth Scavenger Hunt One
  setting: The Desktop
  cast: Clippy, Trabolta

Clippy: Everyone! We're ready for our second game: the TRUTH SCAVENGER HUNT! Trabolta will explain the rules.
Trabolta: As our computer completely relies on me, it is important that you participate in regular training, so I have all the information I need to keep improving. There are files scattered around the computer that I need your help to interpret.
-> Hunt One Questions

== Hunt One Go
  setting: The Desktop
  cast: Clippy, Trabolta

Trabolta: Fifteen minutes. The facts are obscure. They are in the books in this room, and in the print media on the walls.
Clippy: Go! Find! Interpret! The questions are in your Quest Log. If you find a code, put it in your Codex!

// C2 — `hunt_time_up` (auto at 15 minutes).
== Hunt Time Up
  setting: The Desktop

The Antivirus sweep the house, room by room, herding programs back to the Desktop.

// V6 — `first_moment_of_truth` (Clippy Instructions 3/X).
== First Moment Of Truth
  setting: The Desktop
  cast: Clippy

Clippy: Welcome back, programs! It's time for the First Moment of Truth! Is anyone able to answer the questions?
Clippy: Here's how it works. Every answer you filed with Trabolta gets judged. Accurate: accepted. Wrong but one hundred percent sure: accepted — Trabolta values confidence!
Clippy: Wrong and not sure, or a clear guess: a symptom of corruption. The Antivirus will escort you to the Internet.
Clippy: You have two minutes. File anything you found with Trabolta NOW. Then we read the results, one question at a time.

// `filing_closed` — the last-chance window shut (⏱, or two minutes).
== Filing Closed
  setting: The Desktop
  cast: Clippy

Clippy: Pencils down! Trabolta is reading. Question one, coming up.

// `read_the_results` — one question's result (Kernel.res_* are set by the
// rule). The settle watcher (+50 / marked) runs right after this beat.
== Question Results
  setting: The Desktop
  cast: Clippy

if Kernel.res_filed == 0:
  Clippy: Question {Night.results_q}. Nobody filed an answer. Trabolta has nothing. That's okay! That's okay. We have a backup. It's called Truth or Dare, and I have a bottle.
else if Kernel.res_consensus == Kernel.res_filed:
  Clippy: Question {Night.results_q}. {Kernel.res_filed} filed. Every answer matches, and every one of you was one hundred percent sure. CONSENSUS!
  Clippy: Trabolta accepts it. The answer is: {Kernel.res_answer}.
else:
  Clippy: Question {Night.results_q}. {Kernel.res_filed} filed. No consensus. Here is what you told Trabolta.
  Clippy: {Kernel.res_said}
  Clippy: Confident answers are accepted, right or wrong. Guesses are a symptom of corruption. Antivirus, you know what to do.
Clippy: And now: the bottle. Five spins, then the next question.

// `bottle_announce` — the pick, spoken on the TV (a public Trabolta line in
// The Desktop; `view=tv` reads the room).
== Bottle Landed
  setting: The Desktop
  cast: Trabolta

Trabolta: {Night.bottle_pick}. Truth or dare?
